WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.846
[Katherine Dunham] Do not point
your toe. Watch it. That's it.

2
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:28.000
Rachel is someone who should be training
to do roles that I will never do again.

3
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.381
That's fine. I'd like to see you do
this roll at the barre. Remember?

4
00:00:34.381 --> 00:00:39.651
This one where first thing you have to get
yourself lined up, and then you go over,

5
00:00:39.651 --> 00:00:42.190
and you have a contraction, the release.

6
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.000
Then you begin to fall and
recover. Alright, let's see that.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.684
You make this field around you,
and you're the center of it,

8
00:00:50.684 --> 00:00:52.895
and that's all you're interested in.

9
00:00:52.895 --> 00:00:54.000
Alright. Go ahead.

10
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Shoulders down. Alright,
contract. That’s it. And release.

11
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.858
Okay, contract.

12
00:01:02.858 --> 00:01:12.642
Now fall, fall, recover, and two rolls,
and roll, that's it, and fall, recover,

13
00:01:12.642 --> 00:01:13.757
and roll.

14
00:01:13.757 --> 00:01:16.482
Now that's quite good.

15
00:01:16.482 --> 00:01:24.408
Now if you turn to the side, you
can have this fall to the side,

16
00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:28.000
and roll through and come up.

17
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.586
Yes, I've got to see this start, though,
Rachel, as though you were breaking,

18
00:01:38.586 --> 00:01:43.888
so you take a string and just
let it drop, like that, you see?

19
00:01:43.888 --> 00:01:49.789
And that's much better. Yes, and
again. Now stay back there and sink.

20
00:01:49.789 --> 00:01:54.322
Straighten your body line
out and sink to your knees.

21
00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:58.000
Sink to your knees,
that's it, and come up.

22
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.714
All right.

23
00:02:00.714 --> 00:02:03.714
We had the, remember the one you just did,

24
00:02:03.714 --> 00:02:08.071
where you turned into the barre
with your pelvic girdle here.

25
00:02:08.071 --> 00:02:10.929
That must precede you always, that turn.

26
00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:15.143
After you got all the way around,
there's a side extension.

27
00:02:15.143 --> 00:02:20.071
Yeah, with the hip down as far as
possible. That's it. That's better.

28
00:02:20.071 --> 00:02:23.000
Shoulders low, low, low. All right, fine.

29
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.064
And of course, the thing you,

30
00:02:27.064 --> 00:02:34.891
all the time you learn that your hands have this palm
that is part of your isometric resistance and your feet,

31
00:02:34.891 --> 00:02:42.648
the palm of your feet on the floor so that you get
everything that can be gotten from contact with the floor,

32
00:02:42.648 --> 00:02:43.715
with the earth.

33
00:02:43.715 --> 00:02:44.000
See?

34
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.615
[Rachel Tavernier] I enjoy it because it's closer
to me because, you know, Haitian, African,

35
00:02:50.615 --> 00:02:52.385
and drums and all that.

36
00:02:52.385 --> 00:02:54.000
And it was wonderful.

